# Block31 preexecution panel return

This is an author-side five-lens portfolio challenge, not review-loop or an
audit verdict.

| lens | verdict |
|---|---|
| measurement foundations | sample only pointer atoms already proved orthogonal and persistent; do not call the internal class bit a new Record |
| computational theorem | replace all host decoding by a reversible truth circuit and require full mutation sensitivity |
| locality / QCA | exploit the candidate-block geometry itself: eight STATUS samples feed disjoint radial/axial nearest-neighbor rails |
| action / gravity | defer gravity; a source cannot be attached responsibly while the Record-conditioned route is still nonlocal |
| axiom sufficiency | test the constructive physical bridge before considering any axiom amendment; the present gap is implementation, not a demonstrated inconsistency |

Two independent constructive attacks and one prior-art scout agreed that this
is the shortest positive seam.  Existing NN SWAP/CNOT/Toffoli cores are
reusable, but no existing PR implements the comparator or autonomous trigger.
The panel preferred the geometric STATUS relay over a host decoder, a compact
coframe-dependent binary encoder, and an immediate gravity join.

The panel also fixed the claim boundary: Blank-state eligibility can prevent a
second firing in a one-shot CP channel, but a supplied gate-layer schedule is
not cadence or an autonomous cellular law.
